From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xray-studio <xray-studio@localhost>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 05:03:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] app/router: thread an optional decision trace through the
 balancers

Records, per decision: the raw candidate set, the observatory snapshot that was
read, every filter stage with per-candidate rejection reasons and the numbers
behind them, the leastLoad score arithmetic (deviation * sqrt(cost)), the
baseline walk and truncation point, and the final uniform draw.

The traced method IS the normal code path: PickOutbound calls it with a nil
trace and every Trace method is nil-safe. There is deliberately no second
implementation of any balancing algorithm, because a parallel 'explaining' copy
could drift from the real one and the UI would present the drift as truth.

Also surfaces three things upstream has no representation for at all:
  - candidates absent from the observation (leastPing and leastLoad iterate the
    observation, not the candidate list, so an unprobed outbound is invisible
    rather than rejected)
  - that random/roundRobin ignore the observatory entirely unless fallbackTag
    is set, and treat an unobserved candidate as alive
  - that the last step of random and leastLoad is a coin toss, not a ranking
